{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>For every shepherd of sheep is an abomination to the Egyptians.</b> As a sign that in those days the Egyptians did not eat meat, and they would not let a person slaughter sheep, as the people of India do today, and whoever is a shepherd of sheep is an abomination because he drinks the milk, and the people of India do not eat or drink anything that comes from a living creature, even to this day:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:07.559846376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}